# Forms & Validation

## Pattern
- ✅ Keep form state in a controller/notifier when it affects business logic
- ✅ UI-only input state can use controllers locally, but keep it tidy

## Validators
- ✅ Validators live in `domain/` (if business rules) or `shared/validators/`
- ✅ Reuse validators; no duplicated regex across screens

## Controllers
- ✅ Dispose `TextEditingController` and `FocusNode` in `dispose()`
- ✅ Use debouncing for async validations (e.g., username availability)

## Submission
- ✅ Disable submit while loading
- ✅ Show field-level errors and submit-level errors distinctly

## NEVER
- ❌ Validation logic embedded as large lambdas in widgets
- ❌ Fire API calls on every keystroke without debounce/cancel
